SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Art of Coexistence
LOCATION:The Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: You are
  on Waitlist\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/199491\n\
 n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion\nWhat does it mean for humans and w
 ildlife to thrive together in an increasingly interconnected world? Coinci
 ding with the arrival of The Great Elephant Migration in Boston\, this '
 Quin Chat brings together visionary voices at the forefront of conservatio
 n\, research\, and environmental storytelling for an evening of compelling
  conversation.\n\nModerated by 'Quin Co-Founder and philanthropist\, Sandy
  Edgerley\, together with Founder of The Great Elephant Migration\, Ruth G
 anesh and leading scholar of human-wildlife coexistence\, Dr. Tarsh Thekae
 kara\, the discussion will explore the ideas driving one of the world's mo
 st ambitious conservation initiatives.\n\nFrom restoring critical habitats
  and protecting biodiversity to reimagining the relationship between peopl
 e and the natural world\, look forward to a conversation that examines how
  innovation\, collaboration\, and community are reshaping the future of co
 nservation.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only
 . Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly as
 k that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of t
 he event.
